flowchart TB
  accTitle: B1 context assembly and adaptive feedback
  accDescr: Context assembly retrieves candidates, applies non-negotiable eligibility gates, estimates accessibility, task-conditioned set value, and incremental costs, then selects a feasible set under token and elapsed-time budgets. Actual use and task outcomes update later estimates. ACT-R predicted latency and infrastructure wall-clock latency remain separate.
  Q[Query, task, and candidate action] --> R[Candidate retrieval]
  R --> H{Hard eligibility gates}
  H -->|invalid, unsupported, or unauthorized| Z[Reject or quarantine]
  H -->|eligible| F[Build query-time feature snapshot]
  F --> A[Activation and accessibility]
  F --> V[Task-conditioned marginal set value]
  F --> C[Incremental retrieval and context cost]
  F --> L[Latency estimates]
  L --> L1[ACT-R cognitive prediction]
  L --> L2[Measured infrastructure wall-clock]
  A --> S[Set selection and prompt ordering]
  V --> S
  C --> S
  L1 --> S
  L2 --> S
  S --> B{Token and deadline budgets met?}
  B -->|no| T[Reduce set or abstain]
  B -->|yes| W[Insert selected memories into context]
  W --> U[Agent response or action]
  U --> O[Outcome and use evidence]
  O --> UP[Update supported accessibility and value estimates]
  UP -. future query .-> Q
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
